      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T17:09:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing that came up in discussions last year was a preference from Corentin/Michael to avoid having a separate Dawn API for MRSTSS and instead rely on DawnLoadResolveTexture to infer when it can be used. It\u0027s described in https://crbug.com/463893793#comment8 and is discussed a bit in that thread. Skia would still be allocating a transient MSAA texture to use as a color attachment but that texture should be lazily allocated. Internally I believe dawn would replace the color attachment with the single sampled resolve attachment plus MSRTSS struct so the transient MSAA texture isn\u0027t used and is hopefully free/very cheap.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if there was any further discussion on this front?",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
