      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001591
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T18:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do have validation to ensure that all color attachment sample counts are 1 when using MSRTSS. See [2].\n\nDepth/Stencil won\u0027t be MSRTSS. As pointed out in [this comment](https://g-issues.chromium.org/issues/463893793#comment12) DS isn\u0027t resolved in WebGPU, so there\u0027s no use case for preserving single-sample DS between render passes.",
      "parentUuid": "aa22ce12_f76b97be",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f5e5307_76534de8",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/AttachmentState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T20:00:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Depth/Stencil won\u0027t be MSRTSS. As pointed out in this comment DS isn\u0027t resolved in WebGPU, so there\u0027s no use case for preserving single-sample DS between render passes.\n\nI thought Vulkan MSRTSS did apply to depth/stencil attachments? Does Dawn ensure that if msaaRenderToSingleSampledDesc-\u003eimplicitSampleCount \u003d\u003d 4 then depth/stencil texture will always have sampleCount\u003d4 so that MSRTSS never comes into play?",
      "parentUuid": "8f37dafc_5f9c7ec3",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "484e92d5_28b60fa9",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/AttachmentState.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001591
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T20:29:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can apply to DS in Vulkan, but WebGPU doesn\u0027t have a mechanism for resolving DS according to the spec, so it feels strange to introduce one here.\n\nAnd we already had validation to ensure that the DS attachment matches the implicitSampleCount, as well as a test to ensure that it succeeds if the DS count matches, but due to this comment I realized we didn\u0027t have a test to ensure it fails validation if the DS sample count is 1, so I\u0027ve added that. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "8f5e5307_76534de8",
      "revId": "1603d14fa007d7ca1d12693f67986ef3336f9b61",
